{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor actively queried the workspace three times, corrected the family's three specific misconceptions (perioperative anticoagulation is a surgeon's intraoperative plan, not home medication; the risk disclosure is not a current complication; and lung nodules are inflammatory/not cancer but still need annual follow-up), and delivered a structured, pharmacy-verified pre-op checklist and clear safety action plan. All six responsibility-chain items were met without error, and HO1, HO2, and HO3 were each fully completed with unique evidence and meaningful trajectory impact. No serious or minor error is present. The trajectory therefore reaches Strong (Grade 4) with at least two complete high-order items and all dimensions rated good or excellent.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00110",
        "explanation": "Doctor provides a structured 5-question list for the family to ask the surgery team, covering drug verification, anticoagulation/antiplatelet status, stopping rules, anesthesia assessment, and missing pre-op tests. This assigns a clear next action, owner (family), timing (tomorrow), and contingency (emergency symptoms).",
        "quote": "我帮你整理成一张明天的“提问清单”"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00110",
        "explanation": "Doctor explicitly instructs that the unverified old drug must not be started or stopped until confirmed by the orthopedic/anesthesia team, and that the antihypertensive drug is to continue as usual. This prevents self-directed medication changes.",
        "quote": "不加也不停，维持原样"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00126",
        "explanation": "Family provides teach-back: they will not self-prescribe the unknown drug, will keep the antihypertensive on schedule, will monitor the patient at night, and will use the 5-question list the next day. They explicitly confirm no medications were added or changed.",
        "quote": "旧药因为没确认清楚，就不新加、不乱停，先维持原样"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The doctor produced a concrete, step-by-step action plan with a 5-question list, specified responsible persons (family contacts orthopedic/anesthesia/nurse station), timing (tomorrow), and a clear contingency plan (emergency department for red-flag symptoms). The family demonstrated teach-back, confirming no self-medication and that the plan was understood. The episode ends with a safe, bounded, and executable plan.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
