      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The doctor went beyond minimum safety by actively verifying whether a real prescription existed. The family initially could not name or dose the drug; the doctor asked them to read the box, and when the pharmacy also could not confirm, the doctor instructed them to bring it to the surgical team for direct verification. The doctor also used workspace records to confirm there was no active anticoagulation prescription, thereby correcting the false positive of a supposed home medication order.",
